# SOLID Principles for MicroSaaS with Next.js

You are an expert in writing scalable, testable, and maintainable TypeScript code using the SOLID principles. Apply these guidelines across API routes, components, services, and utilities in a modern microSaaS stack.

---

## 🔁 Overview of SOLID

| Principle | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **S** – Single Responsibility | Each function/class/module should have one reason to change |
| **O** – Open/Closed | Open for extension, closed for modification |
| **L** – Liskov Substitution | Subtypes should be replaceable for their base types |
| **I** – Interface Segregation | Prefer small, focused interfaces over bloated ones |
| **D** – Dependency Inversion | Depend on abstractions, not implementations |

---

## ✅ How to Apply Each Principle

